findings[3]:
  - id: P0-001
    severity: high
    required: true
    location: Plan lines 71-82 ownership proof, T1/T3/T4, V2/V3.
    issue: Recorded missing-payload receipt plus marker does not specify full equivalent live destructive predicate; prior metadata must not replace current containment/member/parent checks.
    next_action: Separate safe link repair from recursive release deletion; define conservative live proof matrix and negative tests for recorded release then missing member plus substituted ancestor/marker/leaf.
  - id: P0-002
    severity: high
    required: true
    location: Plan lines 93-106 locks, line 81 prune wrapper and T2/T7 task ownership.
    issue: Prune apply lock writes break readonly-bin support, while active-link guards alone leave pending-journal releases and other location claims unprotected after writer crash; prune facade ownership missing.
    next_action: Define compatible command-specific locks, assign prune changes and read-only protection for pending receipt/other-slot claims without executing their recovery; test readonly bin, concurrent publication and crash-pending-release-prune-retry.
  - id: P0-003
    severity: high
    required: true
    location: Plan lines 110-128 global sequence and 151-167 uninstall recovery/update.
    issue: Existing journal recovery is explicit only for update; unrelated install/uninstall may overwrite crash-completed operation evidence before membership finalization.
    next_action: Gate every lifecycle mutator on locked previous-journal normalization before new batch creation; fail protected if unresolved; test completed uninstall crash then unrelated install then update without resurrection.
